WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.868
-President Trump
is reportedly preparing

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.337
for special counsel
Robert Mueller

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.839
to issue his final report
as early as next week.

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:09.642
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:13.779
♪♪

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:15.948
After Trump declared
a national emergency

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.318
to bypass Congress
and build his border wall,

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:21.387
16 states filed legal challenges
almost immediately.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.189
In comments to reporters
this week,

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.224
Trump insisted
he had the absolute right

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:27.393
to unilaterally build his wall

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.796
and said it was a matter
of national security.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.897
-We have absolute right
to do that.

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:34.334
I have an absolute right
to call national security.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:37.637
We need strong borders.
It's an open and closed case.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:41.107
I was put here for security,
whether it's Space Force,

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:45.077
which we're doing today,
or whether it's borders.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.313
-Space Force and borders.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.982
It's pretty telling
that despite the effects

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:52.585
of climate change, gun violence,
and inadequate healthcare,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.788
Trump thinks
the biggest threats to America

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:57.957
are asylum seekers and Klingons.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.959
I mean, hell,
why not combine the two

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:03.929
and deploy the Space Force
to the border?

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.765
The national...

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.970
The national-emergency
declaration is just the latest

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.573
example of Trump's disregard
for the rule of law.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.041
Republicans have elected a guy

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.876
who tramples over
the Constitution

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.245
after spending years
lecturing the rest of us

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.713
about the Constitution.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.315
And even though
he clearly didn't mean it,

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.517
Trump repeatedly promised
during the campaign

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.486
that he would restore
the rule of law.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:30.390
-We have to restore
the rule of law

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.292
on our border,
in our government.

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.562
No matter where it is,
it has to be restored.

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:40.767
In my administration,
I'm going to enforce all laws

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:46.005
concerning the protection
of classified information.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.407
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:51.411
No one will be above the law.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.246
This election will determine

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:57.116
whether we remain a free country
in the truest sense of the word

00:01:57.116 --> 00:02:00.753
or we become a corrupt
banana republic

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:05.357
controlled by large "derners"
and foreign governments.

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:08.127
-I'm sorry. Real quick.
Can we hear that word again?

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:11.130
-Controlled by large derners.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.633
-Did you mean to say "donors"?

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:17.036
Why do you sound like Madea?

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.705
That's like saying Congress
is going to pass a "ler"

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:22.975
or reminding everyone
to get out and "vert."

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:24.910
But you heard Trump
very clearly there.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.480
The government would not be
controlled by large derners

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.415
or, more importantly,
foreign governments.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.016
The President
of the United States

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:33.686
will put Americans
above everyone else, period.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.489
-In his latest interviews,
as well as in his new book,

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.058
the former FBI acting director
Andrew McCabe

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:42.462
recounts a time President Trump
refused to believe information

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:45.098
from top U.S. intelligence
officials,

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:48.434
preferred instead to take the
word of Russia's Vladimir Putin.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:51.871
-The President said he did not
believe that the North Koreans

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:55.140
had the capability to hit us
here with ballistic missiles

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.476
in the United States.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.943
And he did not believe that

00:02:57.943 --> 00:03:00.913
because President Putin
had told him they did not.

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:03.616
Intelligence officials
in the briefing responded

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:06.752
that that was not consistent
with any of the intelligence

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:09.055
our government possesses.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:13.893
To which the President replied,
"I don't care. I believe Putin."

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.095
-He told American
intelligence officials

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.897
he believed Putin over them.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.333
Say what you will about Trump,
he might be a criminal,

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.335
but at least he's super-obvious
about it.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.236
It's like if someone asked
Barry Bonds

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:26.138
if he wanted to take
batting practice,

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:29.842
and he said, "Not right now.
I have to go take my steroids."

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.544
Why on Earth
would you believe Putin

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.313
over your own
intelligence officials,

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.581
unless you had some sort of
corrupt relationship with him?

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.283
He's not exactly
the most trustworthy guy.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.584
I mean, look at him.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:42.454
That's the same way
Dexter used to smile at people

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:44.390
when they came to
strapped to a table.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.961
You trusted a guy
with resting Dexter face.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.230
In interviews this month,
McCabe has detailed the extent

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.199
to which Trump tried to
interfere in the various

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.134
investigations
of him and his closest aides.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.303
For example,
after Trump fired James Comey

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.605
and McCabe took over
as acting FBI director,

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:03.309
Trump tried to claim
that Comey was widely
disliked within the FBI.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:06.512
And he even tried to get McCabe
to say he also hated Comey,

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.880
which was not true.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.149
-The President
immediately went off

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:13.853
on almost a gleeful description

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:16.589
of what had happened
with the firing of Jim Comey.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.190
And then he went on to state

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.160
that people in the FBI
were thrilled about this,

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.495
that people
really disliked Jim Comey,

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:25.364
and that they were very happy
about this

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:27.133
and that it was a great thing.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:32.205
What I was hearing from
the President was not reality.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:35.107
It was the version of the events

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:38.411
that I quickly realized
he wished me to adopt.

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:42.214
And he said, "I heard
that you were one of the people

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:43.882
that did not support Jim Comey.

00:04:43.882 --> 00:04:45.184
You didn't agree with him

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.219
and the decisions that he made
in the Clinton case.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:50.756
Is that true?"

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:53.425
And I said,
"No, sir, that's not true."

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:55.294
-Trump thinks
he can Jedi mind-trick you

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.628
into believing something.

00:04:56.628 --> 00:04:58.797
He's like one of those
old-timey villains

00:04:58.797 --> 00:05:01.734
with black-and-white swirls
for eyes.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.003
"You hated James Comey."
"No, I liked him."

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.305
"No, you hated him."
"What's wrong with your eyes?"

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:09.175
"Oh, they're transplants.
From a derner."

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.809
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:12.245
McCabe was worried...

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:14.113
[ Applause ]

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.914
McCabe was worried
that the President

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:18.283
was trying to interfere
in the Russia investigation,

00:05:18.283 --> 00:05:19.719
which was obviously true.

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:21.520
In fact, Trump started
to install loyalists

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.756
who he knew he could control,
like his recently departed

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.391
acting attorney general,
Matt Whitaker.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.959
Whitaker refused
to recuse himself

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.994
from the Russia investigation,
and a few weeks ago,

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:31.431
he even insisted the
investigation was winding down,

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:33.566
although he seemed
super nervous about it.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.467
-Before you came
into your current role,

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:36.803
you were publicly very critical

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:38.604
of the special counsel
investigation.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.739
Now since you have received
your briefings,

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:42.842
is there anything
that you've seen or read

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.309
that gives you concern about

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:46.445
special counsel Robert Mueller
or his investigation?

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:48.714
-You know, I've been fully
briefed on the investigation.

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:50.716
And, you know, I look forward

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:55.421
to Director Mueller
delivering the final report,

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.590
but right now, you know,
the investigation is,

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.959
I think,
close to being completed,

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:03.696
and I hope that we can get
the report from Director Mueller

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.465
as soon as we -- as possible.

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:09.234
-Look at how sweaty he is.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:12.872
He looks like a glass of
iced tea on a hot summer day.

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:15.808
Somebody put that guy
on a coaster.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:18.344
Trump installed Whitaker to
get the various investigations

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:20.178
of him and his associates
under control,

00:06:20.178 --> 00:06:22.215
like Michael Cohen,
who was being investigated

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:24.717
by the U.S. Attorney for the
Southern district of New York.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:26.652
And this week,
"The New York Times" reported

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.655
that Trump tried to get Whitaker
to put an ally of his

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.824
in charge of
the Cohen investigation.

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:34.893
-"The Times" reports that while
Manhattan's federal prosecutors

00:06:34.893 --> 00:06:37.496
were gathering evidence
on Trump's involvement

00:06:37.496 --> 00:06:41.467
in hush-money payments
during the 2016 election,

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.302
Trump called former acting

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:45.637
attorney general
Matthew Whitaker.

00:06:45.637 --> 00:06:48.774
"Trump asked
whether Geoffrey S. Berman,

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:50.108
the United States Attorney

00:06:50.108 --> 00:06:53.345
for the Southern district
of New York, and a Trump ally,

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:56.916
could be put in charge
of the widening investigation,

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.985
according to several
American officials

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:01.253
with direct knowledge
of the call."

00:07:01.253 --> 00:07:02.621
-So Trump tried to get Whitaker

00:07:02.621 --> 00:07:04.890
to interfere in the
investigation of Michael Cohen.

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:06.992
Can you imagine
how much Whitaker was sweating

00:07:06.992 --> 00:07:08.794
during that phone call?

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:11.931
Probably looked like
he just climbed out of a pool.

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.233
Now, there's been
speculation for months

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.001
that special counsel
Robert Mueller's investigation

00:07:16.001 --> 00:07:18.704
is wrapping up or winding down,
and it's never been true,

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:20.740
but now this week,
there's new reporting

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.641
that Justice Department
officials are expecting

00:07:22.641 --> 00:07:24.844
Mueller's final report
as soon as next week.

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:26.212
And if that's the case,

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:28.247
it could come when Trump
is out of the country.

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:30.449
-We have the clearest
indication yet

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.218
that special counsel
Robert Mueller

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:35.153
is nearly done with his
almost two-year investigation

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:37.056
and that the end game here
is near.

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:39.425
Sources say the Justice
Department is preparing

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:41.360
to announce
as early as next week

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.962
that Attorney General Bill Barr

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:45.197
has received Mueller's
confidential report.

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:46.932
And soon after
that announcement,

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:49.268
Barr will review the findings

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.937
and then submit his own summary
to Congress.

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:54.706
-If it were released next week,
it would happen

00:07:54.706 --> 00:07:57.242
as the President
was in Hanoi, Vietnam,

00:07:57.242 --> 00:08:01.313
meeting for the second time with
North Korean leader Kim Jong-un.

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:03.949
-So Trump might be
out of the country in Hanoi

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:05.718
when Mueller issues his report.

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:08.788
If that happens,
there's a good chance
Trump just won't come back.

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:11.256
"Kim, you got to smuggle me
back to North Korea.

00:08:11.256 --> 00:08:14.727
Hide me in your coat."

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:16.896
How much more evidence
do we need

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:18.697
that Trump was trying
to obstruct justice?

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:21.200
He told Comey to shut down his
investigation of Michael Flynn.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.668
When Comey refused,
he fired him.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:24.504
He bragged to the Russians
he fired Comey

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:26.171
because of the
Russia investigation,

00:08:26.171 --> 00:08:28.540
and he tried to interfere in the
investigation of Michael Cohen.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.444
The evidence is clear.
When this is all over, Trump
is either gonna go to jail

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:34.246
or he's gonna have to resign
and flee and join the...

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:35.881
-Space Force.

00:08:35.881 --> 00:08:38.050
-This has been "A Closer Look."

